# What runtimes.lua needs from outside Hammerspoon, declared beside the file that names
# these tools. Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason.
# See Olm's lib/deps.lua for the kinds and for how these files are found.
#
# The same three the ports source uses, declared again rather than shared, because a
# declaration belongs beside whatever knows the tool and this file knows them on its own.
# Two owners naming one tool is expected, the manifest carries a line for each and the
# reconciler joins on the name, so nothing is counted twice.
#
# Optional for the same reason as the ports source, see ports.dependencies.
ps   | system | /bin/ps        | optional | finds candidate runtime processes and reads their working directory
lsof | system | /usr/sbin/lsof | optional | checks whether a candidate holds a socket, the evidence that separates a dev server from a stray process
kill | system | /bin/kill      | optional | stops a runtime process, gracefully first and forcefully on request
